ith and without first selecting the node) never changes aria-checked/data-state from \\\"true\\\"/\\\"checked\\\". The competency cannot be disabled via direct interaction, so its exclusion from coverage/gap/critical-path calculations cannot be verified.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Template Library panel lists 5 distinct templates (Software Engineer/Current, Product Manager, HR Manager, Data Scientist, Sales Manager), each showing department, competency count (6), connection count (5), and distinguishing tag chips (e.g. programming/coding vs product/management/strategy vs hr/recruitment/talent), allowing browsing and comparison.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Applying a template produces an inconsistent model - graph not synced with new template data\", \"actual\": \"Clicking \\\\\\\"Apply\\\\\\\" on the Product Manager template correctly updated the page heading to \\\\\\\"Product Manager\\\\\\\", department to \\\\\\\"Product\\\\\\\", Coverage to 78%, Avg Level 3.8, Critical Path list to Product Strategy/User Research/Communication/+1, and the Category Adjustments competency counts (technical 1, behavioral 1, leadership 1, domain 3) - all consistent with a Product Manager model. However the competency graph itself (React Flow nodes/edges) was NOT updated and still rendered the old Software Engineer competencies verbatim (\\\\\\\"Programming Languages\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"System Design\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Code Review\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Problem Solving\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Collaboration\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Agile Methodology\\\\\\\" with the same edges/weights), confirmed via DOM query of .react-flow__node h4 elements. The visual model is inconsistent with the applied template's metadata/metrics.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Saved template not added/retrievable in Template Library\", \"actual\": \"Clicking \\\\\\\"Save Current\\\\\\\" on the Software Engineer model produced a success toast (\\\\\\\"Template Saved - Current model configuration has been saved as a template\\\\\\\"), but the Template Library list was not updated with any new entry - it still shows exactly the same 5 pre-built templates (Software Engineer, Product Manager, HR Manager, Data Scientist, Sales Manager) as before saving. There is no \\\\\\\"My Templates\\\\\\\" section or any other UI location where the newly saved template can be found/retrieved/applied.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Scenario Simulation tabs (Recruitment/Training/Promotion) each render distinct panel content when clicked: Recruitment shows \\\\\\\"Recruitment Simulation\\\\\\\" copy with default Level/Weight Change 0, Training shows \\\\\\\"Training Simulation\\\\\\\" copy with preset +1 Level Change for technical/domain categories, Promotion shows \\\\\\\"Promotion Simulation\\\\\\\" copy with preset -5%/+10% Weight Change for technical/behavioral. Tab aria-selected state correctly moves between tabs.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Simulation produces corrupted (NaN) aggregate metric\", \"actual\": \"On the Software Engineer model (Recruitment tab), setting the \\\\\\\"technical\\\\\\\" category Level Change to +2 via keyboard (ArrowRight on the slider) caused the sibling \\\\\\\"Weight Change\\\\\\\" slider/value for the same category to display \\\\\\\"NaN%\\\\\\\" instead of a numeric value. Clicking \\\\\\\"Run Simulation\\\\\\\" applied the adjustment (Avg Level correctly rose 3.3→4.2 and Critical Path list reordered), but the top-level Coverage metric became \\\\\\\"NaN%\\\\\\\" (was 68%) - a broken aggregate calculation caused by the NaN weight-change value propagating through. \\\\\\\"Reset\\\\\\\" did correctly restore Coverage to 68% and Avg Level to 3.3, and cleared Level/Weight Change back to 0/0%, so Reset itself works, but Run Simulation is not reliably functional.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Save button does not persist edited model state across reload\", \"actual\": \"On the Software Engineer model, the Recruitment tab's \\\\\\\"technical\\\\\\\" category Level Change was set to \\\\\\\"+1\\\\\\\" via keyboard interaction. Clicking the top-toolbar \\\\\\\"Save\\\\\\\" button produced a success toast (\\\\\\\"Model Saved - Your changes have been saved successfully.\\\\\\\"). After reloading the page (http://localhost:6097/) and reopening the Software Engineer model, the Level Change value had reverted to \\\\\\\"0\\\\\\\" (and Weight Change to \\\\\\\"0%\\\\\\\") instead of persisting the \\\\\\\"+1\\\\\\\" that was present before reload/save. The edited state was not restored, meaning Save does not actually persist changes.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Competency Weight sliders declare aria-valuemin=\\\\\\\"10\\\\\\\" and aria-valuemax=\\\\\\\"100\\\\\\\" (checked across all 6 nodes on Software Engineer model), structurally preventing selection of weight values outside 10-100%. Competency Level is restricted to exactly 5 discrete level buttons per node (representing levels 1-5) with no free-text input available, so out-of-range level values cannot be entered via the UI. No numeric text-entry field exists that would allow bypassing these bounds.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Coverage/progress update not correctly tied to real edits; progress bar not determinate\", \"actual\": \"Clicking a competency's enable/disable switch does not toggle its visual checked state (stays aria-checked=\\\"true\\\"/data-state=\\\"checked\\\") yet the Coverage % increments by ~1 on almost every click regardless of which node is clicked, including repeat clicks on the same already-\\